====================
README for Launchpad
====================

Launchpad is an open source suite of tools that help people and teams to work
together on software projects.  Unlike many open source projects, Launchpad
isn't something you install and run yourself (although you are welcome to do
so), instead, contributors help make <https://launchpad.net> better.

Launchpad is a project of Canonical <http://www.canonical.com> and has
received many contributions from many wonderful people.

If you want help using Launchpad, then please visit the Launchpad Manual at:

    https://documentation.ubuntu.com/launchpad/

If you'd like to contribute to Launchpad, have a look at:

    https://documentation.ubuntu.com/launchpad/

Alternatively, have a poke around in the code, which you probably already know
how to get if you are reading this file.


Getting started
===============

There's a full guide for getting up-and-running with a development Launchpad
environment at
<https://documentation.ubuntu.com/launchpad/en/latest/how-to/running/>.  When you are
ready to submit a patch, please consult
<https://documentation.ubuntu.com/launchpad/en/latest/how-to/contributing-changes/>.

Our bug tracker is at <https://bugs.launchpad.net/launchpad/> and you can get
the source code any time by doing:

  $ git clone https://git.launchpad.net/launchpad

See <https://documentation.ubuntu.com/launchpad/en/latest/explanation/navigating/>
for advice on navigating the code.

Firefox in Noble CI
===================

Noble CI pins the official Firefox Snap to a ``core24`` revision in
``.github/scripts/setup-tests.sh``. The tests run Firefox and geckodriver
directly so Firefox can read test pages under ``/tmp``. Newer ``core26``
revisions need a newer glibc when run this way. The pin and refresh hold
apply only to the CI container, not to developer machines.

When changing the pin, validate both a fresh setup and a restored setup
image. The workflow loads a local HTML page in Firefox before running the
full suite and saves the geckodriver log with the other test logs.
